WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.605 --> 00:00:15.773
A baker came out of his shop and stared at the boys.

2
00:00:15.793 --> 00:00:20.917
"Edward, you'd better get back to the tailor shop," said the baker.

3
00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:23.238
"Your master will be angry."

4
00:00:23.258 --> 00:00:27.061
"I don't care," said Edward.

5
00:00:27.081 --> 00:00:29.603
"I was born for the stage.

6
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.464
I don't want to be a tailor!"

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.901
"Are you a tailor?'

8
00:00:36.521 --> 00:00:37.182
asked Vinnie.

9
00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:41.685
"No, I am an apprentice," said Edward.

10
00:00:41.705 --> 00:00:45.188
"Apprentice?" asked Vinnie.

11
00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:50.552
"Young boys need to learn skills for different jobs," said Edward.

12
00:00:50.572 --> 00:00:54.314
"My master, the tailor, is teaching me to sew."

13
00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.256
"Do you like making clothes?"

14
00:00:57.977 --> 00:00:58.657
asked Vinnie.

15
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:01.860
"It's all right," said Edward.

16
00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:05.831
"But my talent is wasted sewing shirts and coats.

17
00:01:06.631 --> 00:01:07.532
I'm an actor!"

18
00:01:07.552 --> 00:01:12.096
"Really?" said Vinnie, impressed.

19
00:01:12.116 --> 00:01:14.898
"Where do you work?"

20
00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:16.840
Edward asked Vinnie.

21
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.204
"Oh, I'm not an apprentice," said Vinnie.

22
00:01:21.224 --> 00:01:22.565
"I go to school."

23
00:01:22.585 --> 00:01:26.408
"You are very lucky," said Edward.

24
00:01:26.428 --> 00:01:30.972
"My family is poor, so I must live with the tailor."

25
00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:37.108
Suddenly, the boys heard a man calling angrily, "Edward!

26
00:01:37.428 --> 00:01:38.269
Where are you?"

27
00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:43.053
"That is my master," sighed Edward.

28
00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:45.174
"I have to go, Vinnie.

29
00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:46.776
I can't practice now.

30
00:01:47.496 --> 00:01:51.099
But someday the queen will see my great talent!"

31
00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:53.201
"What queen?"

32
00:01:53.841 --> 00:01:54.502
asked Vinnie.

33
00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:57.885
"Why, Queen Elizabeth of England!"

34
00:01:58.465 --> 00:01:59.346
cried Edward.

35
00:02:00.347 --> 00:02:01.608
"Queen Elizabeth?"

36
00:02:02.308 --> 00:02:03.788
Vinnie scratched his head.

37
00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:07.009
"Isn't she the queen of England now?"

38
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:08.250
he thought.

39
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.811
Mandy might be able to explain it to him.

40
00:02:12.411 --> 00:02:13.951
But where was his sister?

41
00:02:15.532 --> 00:02:18.192
Meanwhile, Mandy felt like crying.

42
00:02:18.212 --> 00:02:21.093
"How did we get separated?"

43
00:02:21.673 --> 00:02:22.374
she wondered.

44
00:02:22.394 --> 00:02:24.934
"Now I'm all alone.

45
00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.155
How will I get home?"

46
00:02:28.255 --> 00:02:30.996
She lifted her skirt to check her scraped knee.

47
00:02:32.424 --> 00:02:34.905
A carriage drove up alongside Mandy.

48
00:02:36.066 --> 00:02:38.827
A woman wearing a fancy hat looked out.

49
00:02:38.847 --> 00:02:41.008
"Are you all right?"

50
00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:42.568
she asked Mandy.

51
00:02:42.588 --> 00:02:45.490
"Oh, you're bleeding!"

52
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:50.332
"It's okay," Mandy said, sniffing.

53
00:02:50.352 --> 00:02:52.893
"Where do you live?"

54
00:02:53.653 --> 00:02:54.373
asked the woman.

55
00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.895
Mandy bowed her head and didn't answer.

56
00:02:57.915 --> 00:03:00.436
"Let me clean up your knee.

57
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.342
Charles will take you home later," said the woman.

58
00:03:05.483 --> 00:03:08.045
Undecided, Mandy paused for a moment.

59
00:03:08.065 --> 00:03:13.829
"Charles," she said to the driver, "open the door for the little girl."

60
00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:17.551
"Yes, Lady Katherine," replied the driver.

61
00:03:19.252 --> 00:03:22.855
Mandy stared at the woman and then got into the carriage.

62
00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:25.977
"She must be very rich!"

63
00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:27.238
she thought.

64
00:03:27.258 --> 00:03:30.260
"I wish Vinnie could meet her!"

65
00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:35.018
However, Vinnie was seeing a different side of London.

66
00:03:36.138 --> 00:03:38.939
Vinnie and Edward arrived at the tailor shop.

67
00:03:39.679 --> 00:03:44.761
Master Crossland, the tailor, was standing in the door with his hands on his hips.

68
00:03:44.781 --> 00:03:48.483
"So you're hanging out with actors again!"

69
00:03:49.163 --> 00:03:51.224
said the tailor, looking at Vinnie.

70
00:03:51.244 --> 00:03:54.885
"I'm not an actor, sir," said Vinnie.

71
00:03:54.905 --> 00:03:59.807
"In that case, you are welcome, young man," said the tailor.

72
00:03:59.827 --> 00:04:02.962
"Come, it's one o'clock and time to eat.

73
00:04:03.962 --> 00:04:07.065
After lunch, maybe you can help Edward with his work."

74
00:04:08.226 --> 00:04:14.752
The tailor then turned to Edward and said, "When will you stop dreaming of Shakespeare?"
